## 2. NOTIFICATION SYSTEM — STUDENT AND COACH

Build a unified notification center with role-specific content and a consistent visual design.

### 2.1 Notification architecture

Audit the existing Room architecture and extend it with a persistent notification entity if one does not already exist.

A notification should contain, at minimum:

- Unique notification ID.
- Recipient user ID.
- Notification type.
- Title and short message.
- Related entity ID, when applicable.
- Creation timestamp.
- Read/unread status.
- Optional navigation destination or deep-link information.
- An idempotency key to prevent duplicate notifications.

Implement the necessary DAO, repository, ViewModel, and notification UI using the existing architectural conventions.

Notifications must be stored in Room and remain available after navigating away from a screen or restarting the application.

Implement a shared notification center with:

- Unread notification badge.
- Unread count derived from Room.
- Chronological notification list.
- Read/unread visual distinction.
- “Tümünü Okundu İşaretle” action.
- Individual read action.
- Empty state with a clear illustration or icon.
- Relevant navigation when a notification is tapped.
- Appropriate grouping by date where practical.
- Loading, error, and empty states.

Do not display a permanently hardcoded unread count. Update the badge immediately after the underlying notification changes.

Do not delete important notification history merely because a notification has been read.

