## 4. LEVEL PROGRESSION AND LIVE PROGRESS UI

Implement a centralized, testable level configuration. Level is based on cumulative `lifetimeXp`, not the spendable balance.

Use the following initial cumulative thresholds:

| Level | Title | Required lifetime XP |
|---|---|---:|
| 1 | Yeni Başlangıç | 0 |
| 2 | İlk Adım | 100 |
| 3 | Disiplin Yolcusu | 250 |
| 4 | İstikrarlı Öğrenci | 450 |
| 5 | Bilgi Avcısı | 700 |
| 6 | Odak Ustası | 1,000 |
| 7 | Başarı Mimarı | 1,400 |
| 8 | Zirveye Yakın | 1,900 |
| 9 | Mahfaza Ustası | 2,500 |
| 10 | Efsane | 3,200 |

Keep thresholds in one centralized configuration so they can be tuned later without changing multiple screens.

For the current level, calculate:

- XP required to reach the next level.
- XP earned within the current level.
- XP remaining until the next level.
- Percentage progress toward the next level.
- Current level title.
- Next level title.

Use the actual threshold formula:

`levelProgress = (lifetimeXp - currentLevelThreshold) / (nextLevelThreshold - currentLevelThreshold)`

Clamp progress between 0 and 1. At the maximum level, show a completed progress state instead of dividing by a missing next-level threshold.

